      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1922, the school board bought land from the McCall family to build Balsam Grove School, which operated for decades.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25,
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://historictoxaway.org/balsam-grove-community-center/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The historic community center, once a schoolhouse, cracked in half during a 2011 photo session, a story told by long‑time resident Mattie Owen McCall.",
